module v2.test.native_lane_smoke

import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import v2.std.live_tree { LiveTreeDisposition, SubstrateInputsOnly }

// THE required-v2-native LANE'S POSITIVE-POPULATION FLOOR MEMBER (authority:
// gunbc.witness_v2_native_route, clause native_route_positive_population_present). A universe
// in which nothing passes proves the route dead, and exclusion attribution alone cannot see
// that — a route that refuses every member can still be fully owned. So the census requires
// one member to reach NativeTestPassed where the floor expects pass. The body is deliberately
// the grounded fragment only: a Bool literal, the shape the lane's live-verdict control pair
// (v2.native_lane_fixture.control) already proves reaches a verdict — every richer body today
// meets the node grounding frontier (v2.compiler.infer node_grounding_frontier_note) at the
// eval gate, measured 2026-09-10 at 261 members across 110 modules. This member is the
// route's canary, not a stand-in for the frontier: the census's typed exclusion counts carry
// the frontier's size, and as grounding derivation covers more node kinds the positive
// population grows into real tests. It does not retire — at every frontier depth, a route
// that stops reaching verdicts reddens here first.
data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

test fn native_route_positive_population_smoke() -> Bool {
  true
}
